        en: { name: 'Valley of the Beautiful Women', description: 'A horseshoe of dozens of wine cellars cut into a tuff hillside, where winemakers pour Bull’s Blood and white Star of Eger straight from the barrel.', tip: 'Walk 20 minutes from the centre or take the tourist train, and hop from cellar to cellar tasting a glass at each.' },
